# --fix creates the missing CLAUDE.md and skill link, then checks again; a CLAUDE.md with more in it stays for a person
spec: Packs; Fixes
args: --fix --format terse
exit: 1
-- necro.yaml --
version: 0
include: [necro:agent-files]
-- AGENTS.md --
# Top
-- sub/AGENTS.md --
# Sub
-- sub/CLAUDE.md --
@AGENTS.md
More.
-- .agents/skills/a/SKILL.md --
---
name: a
description: x
---
-- @stdout --
necro: fixed 2 hits in 2 files (agent-files/claude-md ×1, agent-files/skill-link ×1); review and re-stage them. Why: necro --explain <rule>
necro: 1 hit can't be fixed automatically:
sub/CLAUDE.md: agent-files/claude-md an AGENTS.md without a CLAUDE.md that imports it
